        "original_id": "b8ae8617-0c2f-5807-8bf6-fddd385b605e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tamzin Outhwaite, Joe Penhall, Dennis Kelly, Mark Little, Emily Watson, Kwame Kwei-Armah, Vicky Featherstone, Torben Betts, Lucinda Coxon, Adam Spreadbury-Maher, Brice Stratford, Simon Fellows, Wesley Snipes\n- Organizations: White Bear Theatre, BBC One\n- Products: EastEnders, Red Cap, New Tricks, 7 Seconds\n- Topics: theatre practitioners, film and television acting\n\nFacts:\n- From 1998 to 2002, Tamzin Outhwaite played Melanie Owen in the BBC One soap opera EastEnders and gained national notice.\n- In 2005, 7 Seconds was released as an American crime film directed by Simon Fellows and starring Wesley Snipes and Tamzin Outhwaite.\n- After EastEnders, Tamzin Outhwaite starred in theatre and television productions including Red Cap and New Tricks.\n- White Bear Theatre has had notable theatre practitioners including Joe Penhall, Dennis Kelly, Mark Little, Emily Watson, Tamzin Outhwaite, Kwame Kwei-Armah, Vicky Featherstone, Torben Betts, Lucinda Coxon, Adam Spreadbury-Maher, and Brice Stratford.",
